            <ArticleTitle>Use of rapid atrial pacing to induce 2:1 atrioventricular block with marked improvement in hemodynamics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rapid atrial pacing by means of temporary atrial pacing wires was used to effect a regular sinus rhythm in a patient with 2:1 atrioventricular block and frequent premature atrial contractions. The change in rhythm allowed effective intra-aortic balloon counterpulsation and markedly improved the hemodynamic situation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
